      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T17:00:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking back at this, there\u0027s a few issues I see with deferring this:\n\n1. The command-line argument `--build-command\u003d` is set during the `c.config` call and is intended to overwrite `os.Args` as the value. If we delay these, it gets a little nasty to check whether it\u0027s already been set and then setting it with osArgs if nil.\n\n2. `met` seems to be necessary for logger instantiation in config and buildCtx. It might be possible to refactor this out, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s appropriate for this CL. I agree that the overhead is a little confusing for some. Maybe let\u0027s add some //TODO clean this up for upload-metrics-only ?",
